<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganghwa Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ganghwado</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ganghwa Island is an island at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incheon">Incheon</a>. From 1232 to 1270 it sheltered the Goryeo court from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, who could not cross its narrow straits. In the 1860s and 1870s it was attacked by French and American expeditions, and the Japan-Korea Treaty of 1876 was signed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ganghwa-island.jpg" alt="Ganghwa Island" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Davidinkorea at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ganghwa1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
